    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d768">

                <pb facs="0682" n="672" xml:id="pg672"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">124.93/2–149: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-02-01T13:00:00+01:00">February 1, 1949—1
                            p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 7:37 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>395. According Foreign Office, Soviet Ambassador, Nanking, informed French
                    Ambassador January 30, he had received instructions to accompany Chinese
                    Government to Canton. We had previously informed Foreign Office contents Deptel
                    104, January 26 to Nanking, repeated Paris 236, and Foreign Office would
                    appreciate being informed whether we contemplate any changes as result Soviet
                        decision.<anchor n="30" xml:id="d768-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d768-f1" n="30" xml:id="d768-f1-content">
                <p>In his telegram No. 321, February 3, 5 p. m., the Secretary of State responded
                    that the Department did not contemplate any change.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
